":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land — Swamp"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Flying"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Wind Drake","oracle_id":"d6ffdaf0-ac08-4de9-bbce-2eab2f86bcca","oracle_text":"Flying","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2016-09-30","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature — Drake"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Split second"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}{R}{R}","name":"Word of Seizing","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","oracle_text":"Split second (As long as this spell is on the stack, players can't cast spells or activate abilities that aren't mana abilities.)\nUntap target permanent and gain control of it until end of turn. It gains haste until end of turn.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-11-20","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If, during a player's declare attackers step, a creature is tapped, is affected by a spell or ability that says it can't attack, or hasn't been under that player's control continuously since the turn began (and doesn't have haste), then it doesn't attack. If there's a cost associated with having a creature attack, the player isn't forced to pay that cost, so it doesn't have to attack in that case either.","oracle_id":"8aae6f84-02ac-4f8f-9721-b12138588b6b","published_at":"2013-09-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of each attacking creature still chooses which player or planeswalker that creature attacks.","oracle_id":"8aae6f84-02ac-4f8f-9721-b12138588b6b","published_at":"2013-09-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The last ability affects creatures that are already attacking when it resolves. Activating it before combat won't affect any creatures that attack later that turn.","oracle_id":"8aae6f84-02ac-4f8f-9721-b12138588b6b","published_at":"2013-09-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"After a spell with split second resolves (or otherwise leaves the stack), players may again cast spells and activate abilities before the next object on the stack resolves.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Casting a spell with split second won't affect spells and abilities that are already on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the resolution of a triggered ability involves casting a spell, that spell can't be cast if a spell with split second is on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players may turn face-down creatures face up while a spell with split second is on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players still get priority while a card with split second is on the stack; their options are just limited to mana abilities and certain special actions.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Split second doesn't stop triggered abilities from triggering, such as that of Chalice of the Void. If one does, its controller puts it on the stack and chooses targets for it, if any. Those abilities will resolve as normal.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
